  {
   "id": 242834,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/b877fa2b08ab67b4.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work from World Ocean Review)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The image shows carbon reservoirs and carbon cycling. The red numbers represent changes to the carbon cycle due to human activities. The numbers near the arrows are yearly changes, while the numbers in the reservoir represent total change over many years.</p>\n<p>What is the greatest reservoir for carbon on Earth?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 760797,
     "content_html": "The atmosphere."
    },
    {
     "id": 760796,
     "content_html": "The fossil fuels."
    },
    {
     "id": 760798,
     "content_html": "The oceans."
    },
    {
     "id": 760795,
     "content_html": "The vegetation."
    }
   ],
